  "finding": "The tested legal-action sets and transitions are distributionally equivariant under branch-label permutations. Replacing raw stable-key tie-breaks with symmetric action-orbit sampling changed round kind in 19/360 pairs (5.28%) in each mix and changed the finish winner in 21.4% and 23.7% of pairs where both arms finished. This is tie-break/representation sensitivity, not evidence that the orbit policy is strategically stronger.",
